# P5-004 additive skill-goal contract

Owner approved the compatibility proposal on 2026-10-27 (ADR-027). `schemaVersion: 1`, IndexedDB database/version/store/key and browser origin remain unchanged. There is no eager migration, normalization or bulk rewrite on load/import. Goals without this attribute (or with null) remain freeform. Existing Prayer category remains valid; it is omitted only from new-category choices.

New structured Skill goals carry optional `skillGoal: {"format":1,"skillId":"osrs:skill:prayer","targetLevel":70}`. The format and exact keys are validated; skill ID must match the bounded 24-skill rule set, level must be an actual JSON integer 1–99, and category must be Skill. Missing/null level, strings, fractions, out-of-range levels, unknown skill IDs/formats or incompatible categories reject without mutation. Creation never defaults to level 1. Skill and level generate the title; structured edits regenerate it. Completion remains manual and is never inferred from level or archived counters.

The attribute is independent from existing hidden `progress.current/target`; those values are retained exactly. No title parsing converts freeform Skill goals. Legacy Prayer goals remain editable/filterable/reloadable/importable without conversion. Quick and detailed editors provide skill/level controls only when the goal already has valid structured data; a new goal gets it through the Skill picker. Existing freeform Skill editing stays freeform. Structured category/title are generated/locked in these editors; normal notes/status editing remains available. The original `catalogRef` snapshot remains preserved during subsequent structured edits, while `skillGoal` is the structured authority; dictionary changes do not rewrite either automatically.

Current create/edit validation, shared history, cloning, IndexedDB and JSON backups preserve the optional attribute and every existing reference/override/counter/ID. Import validates detached candidates before existing preview/export-required/replacement-confirmation handling. Failed saves/replacements preserve the previous committed document; Retry uses existing behavior. Malformed attributes do not trigger reset/recovery deletion. Export a known-good current JSON/package before switching builds.

Compatibility limit: older schema-1 builds may retain unknown object fields through their generic cloning/export, but they do not understand this attribute, validate its meaning, or offer structured editors. Freeform edits in older builds may leave title/skill metadata inconsistent. Use the current build for structured goals; retain the original package and JSON for rollback. No cross-version editing guarantee, automatic down-conversion or lossy export is claimed. Loading legacy data in the current build leaves missing attributes missing; saving an unrelated field does not create one.
